Regexp.timeout is 2.0 seconds; hitting it is reported as the exception class.

patterns with no backreference, ruby:
  ^(a+)+$                  120 a's then '!'       no match
  ^(a|a)*$                 120 a's then '!'       no match
  ^(\s*|\t)+$              120 spaces then '!'    no match
  ^(\w+\s?)*$              120 a's then '!'       no match
  ^([a-z]{2,4})+$          120 a's then '!'       Regexp::TimeoutError
  the email regex          a@a. 120 a's then '!'  Regexp::TimeoutError

the same engine, with the pattern changed instead:
  ^(?>a+)+$                120 a's then '!'       no match
  ^([a-z]{2,4})++$         120 a's then '!'       no match
  the email regex, fixed   a@a. 120 a's then '!'  no match
